## 10. Termination

### 10.1 Termination for breach

If the Licensee breaches this Agreement, the Licensor may provide written notice describing the breach.

The Licensee will have thirty (30) calendar days from receipt of the notice to remedy the breach, where the breach is capable of remedy.

If the Licensee fails to remedy the breach within that period, the Licensor may terminate this license by written notice.

### 10.2 Serious violations

Nothing in this Section prevents the Licensor from seeking immediate legal or equitable relief where necessary to address ongoing infringement, unauthorized public distribution of engine source code, or other serious violations for which a delay would cause material harm, subject to applicable law.

### 10.3 Effects of termination

Upon termination, the Licensee must cease using Lynx Engine and any Modified Engine to the extent required by the termination notice and applicable law, and must stop any prohibited distribution of the engine or its source code.

Termination does not automatically prohibit continued distribution of previously developed Games that comply with this Agreement, provided that the Licensee continues to meet applicable royalty, reporting, intellectual property, and other surviving obligations.

Any royalties accrued before termination remain payable. Sections intended by their nature to survive termination will remain in effect.

